<main id="main-content" class="world-page love-page"><section class="world-hero ghx-wrap" aria-labelledby="love-title"><div class="love-hero-inner"><p class="ghx-kicker">The relationship behind the work</p><h1 id="love-title">The Woman<br/>Behind the Scenes.</h1><p class="world-lead">Meet GhostHeart’s Rebel.</p></div></section>
<section class="world-prose ghx-wrap" aria-labelledby="love-stayed-title"><div class="world-section-label">A story already present in the songs</div><div class="world-prose-grid"><div><h2 id="love-stayed-title">The Woman Behind the Scenes</h2></div><div class="world-reading"><p>I was confused about love.</p>
<p>Some people held hands and made it look easy. Others said they screamed because they cared. Some of what people called love left bruises. Some love left.</p>
<p>I didn’t understand how all of that could live under the same word.</p>
<p>But I knew what I wanted.</p>
<p>I wanted my grandparents’ love.</p>
<p>Married within six months. Kids. A house. Fifty-four years together. From where I stood, they always worked as a team. I didn’t see yelling or fighting. I saw two people who made loving each other look like the easiest thing in the world.</p>
<p>They were perfect to me.</p>
<p>I wanted that. I just didn’t understand that I could spend my life looking for their love and miss the love standing right in front of me.</p>
<p>Because I’m not my grandpa. And my life didn’t look like his.</p>
<p>I knew my momma loved me. I knew I could give somebody my whole heart. But giving everything I had didn’t mean I knew how to love well. I was still learning how to be the man I wanted to be. How to be a good husband. How to recognize love when it asked something difficult of me.</p>
<p>I hadn’t understood that love could fight for you. That sometimes it meant helping you stand, and sometimes it meant challenging what you were standing for.</p>
<p>Then my wife took my hand, and it felt like a whole new universe.</p>
<p>In GhostHeart’s world, you’ll know her as GhostHeart’s Rebel.</p>
<p>There’s a whole story in how we found each other. We’ll get there. This one begins with the challenge Rebel put in front of me.</p>
<p>I wanted to help people like me. Build a place for the broken ones. The people whose pain I recognized because I’d carried some of it myself.</p>
<p>I thought that was where change began.</p>
<p>Rebel made me look at who I was leaving outside.</p>
<p>If I wanted the world to stop separating people, why was I building another line between us? What about the people whose lives I didn’t understand? The ones who didn’t look like me, love like me, or carry the same scars?</p>
<p>Did they deserve less kindness because their pain wasn’t familiar?</p>
<p>That got to me.</p>
<p>I had been telling her how much I cared. How angry I was. How badly I wanted the world to change. Rebel challenged me to make that care bigger than the people I already knew how to stand beside.</p>
<p>Everyone needed love. Everyone needed room to be human. If I wanted to bring people together, I had to mean it when somebody different walked through the door.</p>
<p>And I had to do more than tell her about it.</p>
<p>I had to tell the world. More than that, I had to start showing it.</p>
<p>She got to me.</p>
<p>I wanted to make a change. Rebel made me face where that change had to begin.</p></div></div></section>
